    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "For additive selection $ (h = 0) $, this has a simple solution of $$ p_{t}=\\frac{p_{0}}{p_{0}+(1-p_{0})e^{-st}} $$ where $ p_t $ is the frequency of allele $ A $ at time $ t $. Often of greater interest is $ t_{p_t,p_0} $, the expected time required to move from initial frequency of $ p_0 $ to target value of $ p_t $. From Equation 5.3a, this is given by the integral $$ t_{p_{t},p_{0}}=\\frac{1}{s}\\int_{p_{0}}^{p_{t}}\\frac{dx}{x(1-x)[1+h(1-2x)]} $$",
      "source_page": 113,
      "source_pages": [
        113
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
