    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Crow and Kimura (1970) presented explicit results for several important cases. If fitnesses are additive $ (h = 0) $ $$ t_{p_{t},p_{0}}\\simeq\\frac{1}{s}\\ln\\left(\\frac{p_{t}\\left(1-p_{0}\\right)}{p_{0}\\left(1-p_{t}\\right)}\\right) $$ whereas if A is recessive $ (h = -1) $ $$ t_{p_{t},p_{0}}\\simeq\\frac{1}{2s}\\left[\\ln\\left(\\frac{p_{t}\\left(1-p_{0}\\right)}{p_{0}\\left(1-p_{t}\\right)}\\right)-\\frac{1}{p_{t}}+\\frac{1}{p_{0}}\\right] $$ and finally, if A is dominant $ (h = 1) $ $$ t_{p_{t},p_{0}}\\simeq\\frac{1}{2s}\\left[\\ln\\left(\\frac{p_{t}\\left(1-p_{0}\\right)}{p_{0}\\left(1-p_{t}\\right)}\\right)+\\frac{1}{1-p_{t}}-\\frac{1}{1-p_{0}}\\right] $$",
      "source_page": 113,
